# 6. LIVE GPS LOCATION TRACKING

Implement controlled GPS tracking during active attendance sessions.

This feature is important for construction workforce coordination and site attendance monitoring.

## Tracking Rules

1. Location tracking starts only after an authorized active check-in.
2. Tracking continues during the authorized work session.
3. Target location update interval is every five minutes.
4. Tracking stops after successful check-out.
5. Tracking must not continue outside the authorized work session.
6. Employees must be informed that tracking is active.
7. Provide a visible tracking indicator.
8. Show the last successful update time.
9. Record location accuracy.
10. Support offline location queues where technically possible.
11. Synchronize queued records securely when connectivity returns.
12. Mark delayed or stale location updates clearly.

## Tracking Screen

Display:
- Active tracking status.
- Assigned site.
- Current location, where available.
- Last update time.
- GPS accuracy.
- Work session duration.
- Site geofence status.

Use an interactive map when location permission is available.

Clearly label the current location and assigned site.

If location permission is unavailable, show a useful status message instead of fake coordinates.

## Privacy and Platform Limitations

Tracking must be transparent and limited to authorized work sessions.

Do not secretly track employees outside working hours.

Explain why location access is required.

Support Android background location permissions where approved.

On iOS and Android, respect operating-system background execution limitations. Do not promise uninterrupted five-minute background updates in every situation.

Use best-effort native background tracking, offline queues, visible tracking state and last-update indicators.

Provide an appropriate attendance exception workflow when location tracking fails.

Apply configurable data retention and access permissions.

Only authorized supervisors and managers should view employee location information for legitimate operational purposes.

